    "turn_text": "Well, I do. I think I've been kind of on the forefront of all of this. I think I was the first person and it might have been back in 2011. It might have been 2010. It's been a long time back. They call out the tea party for what they were. They came to Washington and they demonstrated and protested and spat up on John Lewis or Emmanuel Cleaver coming up to the Capitol and I went among them. I put on some shades and a baseball cap and was listening to my tunes on my pod and walked among them and looked at them and I could see they were the same type of people that had thrown rocks at the state Capitol during the income tax issue that had come up in Tennessee, provoked by Marcia Blackburn, who rallied him up there, and they caused chaos. And it was just the same anti-tax, anti-government borderline racist people that had seen for years in Tennessee. And it was the same people up there at the United States Capitol that were the Tea Party folks. And then I've been out there on the front lines on Trump and this Republican Congress, which has maybe been the worst, 150th Congress ever. running interference for Trump, helping him and being complicit with him, and what I think is going to be shown to be one of the great crimes of the history of mankind. The presidential candidate involved with the Russians, I think that's going to be shown by Robert Mueller.",
