    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75001.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "It's hard to say when I first did. I guess we had suspicions early in his administration And there were, you know, I don't think anybody realized it necessarily during the election. Although, you know, I remember being shocked when he had one of his speeches at Russia, if you're listening, whatever it was, 30,000 emails. And there were some other things that came up concerning the changes in the Republican Party's platform concerning giving Ukraine offensive weapons. And there were certain evidences that were out there. But it wasn't, I guess, until We started this Congress and his presence began and you started to see so many connections. And I guess early on, it was, and it might have been before they took office when Kushner was trying to get a back channel to the White House from Russia. And you know, what is going on here? And all the contacts with Kislyak, with Sessions, with Flynn, you name it. It's so obvious that They weren't good hoots, and then the more and more it goes on and the more you learn, it's so obvious that you know",
